`SqlMapperAsync` contains 6 calls to native ADO (`cmd.ExecuteReaderAsync`, `cmd.ExecuteNonQueryAsync` and `cmd.ExecuteScalarAsync`)

Each call could be made by an `ExecAsync` method that call the listeners:

```csharp
var cmd = conn.CreateCommand();
// prepare cmd
var i = Exec(cmd, (cmd) => cmd.ExecuteNonQueryAsync());
````

```csharp
static async Task<T> ExecAsync<T>(DbCommand command, Func<DbCommand, Task<T>> func)
{
    if(!Listeners.Enabled) return func(command);

    foreach (var (action, failOnError) in Listeners.BeforeExecutionListeners)
    {
        try
        {
            action(command);
        }
        catch
        {
            if (failOnError)
            {
                throw;
            }
        }
    }
    try
    {
        Stopwatch sw = Stopwatch.StartNew();
        T result = await func(command);
        long elapsedTime = sw.ElapsedMilliseconds;
        foreach (var (action, failOnError) in Listeners.AfterExecutionListeners)
        {
            try
            {
                action(command, result, elapsedTime);
            }
            catch
            {
                if (failOnError)
                {
                    throw;
                }
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
    catch (Exception e)
    {
        try
        {
            Listeners.AfterExceptionListeners.ForEach(listener => listener(command, e));
        }
        catch
        {
        }
        throw;
    }
}
```

Upon doing a bit more digging into the Npgsql source, I believe this is indeed a bug in their `PolymorphicArrayConverter<T>` implementation. The other converters I've seen specify the number of bytes that must be read-ahead in a `CanConvert` that looks something like this (this example is for `Guid`s):

```csharp
public override bool CanConvert(DataFormat format, out BufferRequirements bufferRequirements)
{
    bufferRequirements = BufferRequirements.CreateFixedSize(16 * sizeof(byte));
    return format is DataFormat.Binary;
}
```

`PolymorphicArrayConverter<T>` does not override `CanConvert`, despite unconditionally reading at least 8 bytes any time it is used.

Opening an issue in Npgsql.

