If that fix is working, it is working by accident; the "good" version should be:

``` c#
 for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++)
{ 
    await PostgresqlQueryAsync(conn, transaction);
}
```

with

``` c#
private async Task PostgresqlQueryAsync(NpgsqlConnection conn, IDbTransaction  transaction)
{...}
```

The `await` is important; without that, as Nick says, you're overlapping work on `conn` / `transaction`, and that *isn't expected* (by Npgsql - this isn't a Dapper thing, it is a fundamental consideration of ADO.NET connections).

As a tip: any time you see `async void`, there's a high probability that you're doing something very very wrong.

