For anyone else running into this.  If you use `datetime2` exclusively, you can fix the issue by overriding Dapper's defaults.

```
// dapper assumes C# DateTime is SQL DateTime, but we want DateTime2
SqlMapper.AddTypeMap(typeof(DateTime), DbType.DateTime2);
```

If you mix `datetime` and `datetime2`, then you will need a more granular approach, like Marc suggested.

DbString can be used to configure more specific string parameter types.
This might be what you need here.

