To pop back up to your direct goal: that isn't how tokens are supposed to work. You'd pass a linked token into Dapper. Unfortunately, we didn't do these API parameters correctly everywhere in the current version and it's a fairly large break to do them now. In Dapper v2 all `*Async` methods will properly take a `CancellationToken` directly, so all of the async behavior just works as you'd expect. So this is definitely our fault, but we'll address it the next major release (due to the breaking nature).

